2. WHAT "NON-COMMERCIAL" MEANS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A use is NON-COMMERCIAL if it is not primarily intended for, or directed
toward, commercial advantage or monetary compensation.

The following are COMMERCIAL USE and are NOT granted by this license:

  (a) selling, sublicensing, renting or licensing the Software or a
      Derivative Work, or bundling it into a product or service that is sold
      or licensed;
  (b) offering the Software or a Derivative Work to others as a paid or
      ad-supported service, including hosting, SaaS, "music/podcast platform
      as a service", white-label or managed deployments;
  (c) operating it as part of the business of a for-profit company or for the
      benefit of a for-profit company (including internal use by employees
      in the course of their work), or as part of any activity intended to
      earn revenue;
  (d) running it with subscriptions, paywalls, paid tiers, advertising,
      sponsorship, affiliate links, or any other mechanism that earns money
      from the people who use it or from their attention or data;
  (e) charging for installation, deployment, customisation, support or
      training that consists of, or is built around, the Software;
  (f) using the Software, its code or its design to train or build a
      competing commercial product or service.

Voluntary donations to an otherwise non-commercial, non-profit project that
are not tied to access or features are not, by themselves, commercial use.
If you are unsure whether your use is commercial, ask first (see section 3).

